//! The genesis package: laws a world writes itself. A law is a document
//! like any other; a world writes one as an output `to files` into a
//! directory the person running it allowed, and the session reads it,
//! compiles it and puts it in its law's place, or refuses it and keeps
//! the law before it running (an input `= checks` says why).
//!
//! A world rarely writes a law letter by letter: it fills one written
//! beforehand. A template is a law's text with holes, `$0` to `$9`,
//! each filled with a number the world computed; `graphs/law.esn`
//! fills one and gives the operation that writes it.
package genesis@1 { language = 1; ir = 1; }

use "kernels/";
